              "start_index": 2941,
              "end_index": 3068,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Additionally, the signed Declaration of Solvency must be filed with Companies House within 15 days of the winding-up resolution"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              8,
              16,
              14
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3070,
              "end_index": 3140,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "The appointed liquidator will also formally notify any known creditors"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              8,
              0,
              1,
              12,
              13,
              4,
              6
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3248,
              "end_index": 3525,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Their responsibilities include ceasing all trading operations, collecting and realising all company assets, settling all outstanding creditor claims (including any contingent liabilities), and undertaking all necessary administrative and legal paperwork, particularly with HMRC"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              13,
              6,
              7
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3527,
              "end_index": 3669,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "A critical step is obtaining formal clearance from HMRC regarding PAYE, VAT, and Corporation Tax to ensure all financial matters are concluded"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              8,
              1,
              12,
              13,
              4,
              6
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3676,
              "end_index": 3854,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "**Distribution to Shareholders**\n    Once all debts and the costs of liquidation have been paid in full, any remaining surplus funds are distributed to the company's shareholders"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              8
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3856,
              "end_index": 3926,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "In straightforward cases, shareholders may receive early distributions"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              10,
              11
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3933,
              "end_index": 4164,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "**Final Meeting and Company Dissolution**\n    After the company's affairs are fully wound up, the liquidator prepares a final account of the liquidation, detailing how it was conducted and how the company's property was disposed of"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              11
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4166,
              "end_index": 4301,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "A final general meeting of the company is convened for the liquidator to present this account to the members and provide an explanation"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              13
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4303,
              "end_index": 4377,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Following this, the liquidator files the final report with Companies House"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              8,
              0,
              1,
              16,
              12,
              13,
              6
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4379,
              "end_index": 4522,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "The company is then officially dissolved and removed from the Companies House Register, typically three months after this final report is filed"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              8,
              16,
              13,
              3,
              14,
              5,
              9,
              7
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4553,
              "end_index": 4664,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "The full timeline for a Members' Voluntary Liquidation in the UK typically ranges from **six months to a year**"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              8,
              3,
              14
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4666,
              "end_index": 4830,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "However, this duration can vary significantly based on the complexity of the business, the nature of its assets, and the efficiency of the asset realisation process"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              14
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4833,
              "end_index": 5056,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   For companies with very simple assets and ownership structures, where all liabilities are already settled and all necessary paperwork is readily available, the process might be completed in as little as **three months**"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              14,
              7
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 5058,
              "end_index": 5164,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   More complex situations are generally expected to take **6-12 months**, and in some cases, even longer"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              13
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 5167,
              "end_index": 5278,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Specific elements within the timeline include:\n*   Preliminary preparations and financial assessment: 1-2 weeks"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              13
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 5280,
              "end_index": 5318,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   Declaration of Solvency: 1-2 weeks"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              13
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 5320,
              "end_index": 5404,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   Board meeting and shareholders' resolution: 1-2 weeks (including notice periods)"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              0,
              14,
              4
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 5406,
              "end_index": 5483,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   Advertisement in The Gazette: within 14 days of the winding-up resolution"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              0,
              14
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 5485,
              "end_index": 5585,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   Filing Declaration of Solvency with Companies House: within 15 days of the winding-up resolution"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              13
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 5587,
              "end_index": 5657,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   Asset realisation and debt repayment by the liquidator: 2-4 months"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              13
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 5659,
              "end_index": 5703,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   Distribution to shareholders: 4-6 months"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              13,
              7
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 5705,
              "end_index": 5740,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   Clearance from HMRC: 6-9 months"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              13
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 5742,
              "end_index": 5899,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   Final report and company dissolution: The company is officially dissolved approximately three months after the final report is filed with Companies House"
            }
          }
        ],
